:{{tx}}
:'''Feixiao:''' Generals, I am finished with my questioning.
:'''Huaiyan:''' So, what do you think, General Feixiao? Have the doubts in the report been cleared up?
:'''Feixiao:''' The two Nameless have been honest in their answers. Even though there are some tricky details, my intuition tells me there is nothing wrong.
:'''Feixiao:''' However, the three questions I posed earlier were not just for the Nameless, but for you too, General Jing Yuan.
:'''Feixiao:''' First, the Disciples of Sanctus Medicus grew uninterrupted on the Luofu, yet the Six Charioteers were not aware of it. That was a dereliction of duty.
:'''Feixiao:''' Second, you believed in the Stellaron Hunters' prophecy and entrusted outsiders to solve the crisis, even granting them access to the plaguemark. That was a dereliction of responsibility.
:'''Feixiao:''' Third, you insist on holding the Wardance right after the Ambrosial Arbor Crisis, putting the Luofu back in the spotlight. That is a dereliction of wisdom.
:'''Huaiyan:''' Merlin's Claw, is this your line of thinking... or the Ten Lords'?
:'''Feixiao:''' From the moment I walked in, I made it clear that {{Цвет|Ключевой|nobold=1|the questions I'd ask might not reflect my actual thoughts}}.
:'''Jing Yuan:''' ...The Disciples of Sanctus Medicus were deeply rooted and had been plotting for a long time. I admit it was my negligence for not noticing it earlier.
:'''Jing Yuan:''' As for the Stellaron Hunters' prophecy, I didn't believe all of it, but in the end, the Luofu did survive the Ambrosial Arbor crisis. So, I think it's safe to say that Elio's prophecy about the future holds some merit.
:'''Jing Yuan:''' And as for the Wardance... Do you think I'm unaware of the risks? However, risks can also be opportunities. The Luofu has lain low for too long. I believe it's time to stir up the dregs hidden in the depths and wash them away once and for all.
:'''Feixiao:''' Just as I expected from our sophisticated Divine Foresight. You have a way with words. I like it.
:'''Feixiao:''' But unfortunately, ever since the report was submitted, the Alliance has been filled with rumors and speculation. Even within the Luofu, there are people accusing you of neglecting your duties, resulting in the Ambrosial Arbor's resurrection.
:'''Jing Yuan:''' So, what are your thoughts on all of this, General Feixiao?
:'''Feixiao:''' As a fellow Arbiter-General, I fully understand the difficulties of this position.
:'''Feixiao:''' Personally, I think all these rumors are meaningless drivel. Across the sea of stars, the Divine Foresight knows better than anyone else what happened on the Luofu and the meaning behind it...
:'''Feixiao:''' ...Just as what happened on the Xianzhou Yaoqing recently.
:'''Jing Yuan:''' You mean, the Xianzhou Yaoqing is also...?
:'''Feixiao:''' The scouts of the Verdant Knights have sent back reports that borisin are making trouble again. The borisin packs that were once divided and scattered have started swallowing each other up, forming larger and larger packs. Moreover, there's an entity named "Mangas" behind it all.
:'''Huaiyan:''' An "entity"?
:'''Feixiao:''' According to the report, this entity... isn't actually a borisin. It's a woman claiming to be the Messenger of the Master of Immortality. She's described as having "twelve faces and twelve pairs of fangs, as cruel as poison and as elusive as quicksand." The borisin believe she'll give them a chance to rise again.
:'''Jing Yuan:''' That's Phantylia.
:'''Feixiao:''' That's right.
:'''Feixiao:''' You're lucky that I'm the one who came this time. If it were {{Rubi|the Patina Justice|Youwu}} or {{Rubi|the Seer Strategist|Yao Guang}}, this conversation might not be so friendly.
:'''Feixiao:''' I've always had faith in my instincts, so I don't doubt your good intentions. But the Alliance has its fair share of questions and doubts about the Luofu. So, my plan is to come up with an acceptable answer to satisfy the Alliance.
:'''Jing Yuan:''' What's in this plan, General Feixiao?
:'''Feixiao:''' General Jing Yuan, you already know what has to be done, but since you don't want to be the bad guy, I'll take care of it for you. You need the final word from the Ten-Lords Commission to quell any doubts.
:'''Feixiao:''' And for that, I'll have to ask the two Nameless to visit the Shackling Prison.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Are you imprisoning us?
:'''Feixiao:''' No, I'm not imprisoning you. While you're there, I'll ask a judge in the Ten-Lords Commission's Interrogation Division to record a detailed testimony with the Karmic Mirror from both of you. We'll fill in the gaps that weren't covered in the report and silence any protests within the Alliance.
